From cb343dd58f476dd78fc547a04753402dcaabf6f1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Navid Ghahremani <ghahramani.navid@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 21:25:56 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] sanechips: add support for ZTE ZXHN H3600

The ZTE ZXHN H3600 (also known as H1600 variant) is an 802.11ax
(Wi-Fi 6) residential gateway powered by the Sanechips
ZX279128S dual-core ARM Cortex-A9 SoC.

Hardware Specifications:
- SoC: Sanechips ZX279128S (2x ARM Cortex-A9 @ 1.0 GHz, ARMv7-A)
- RAM: 512 MiB DDR3
- Flash: 256 MiB SPI-NAND (Winbond W25N02KV)
- WLAN: 2.4/5 GHz DBDC 2T2R / 4T4R 802.11ax (MediaTek MT7915D PCIe)
- Ethernet: 5x 10/100/1000 Mbps (4x LAN GbE, 1x WAN GbE)
  - switch: Sanechips integrated Gigabit Ethernet switch
- LEDs/Buttons (GPIO): 7x / 3x (Reset, WPS, Lights toggle)
- UART: 3-pin pads on PCB
  - assignment: 3.3V TTL, GND, TX, RX
  - settings: 115200n8
- Power: 12 VDC, 1.5 A

Flash Instructions:

1. Connect 3.3V USB-TTL serial converter to UART pads (115200 8N1).
2. Interrupt bootloader at prompt: press any key to enter cspboot.
3. Configure TFTP network environment:
     setenv ipaddr 192.168.1.1
     setenv serverip 192.168.1.100
4. Place openwrt-sanechips-zx279128s-zte_zxhn-h3600-initramfs-kernel.bin
   on TFTP server as "h3600-initramfs.bin".
5. Load and boot initramfs image over TFTP:
     tftp 0x82000000 h3600-initramfs.bin
     bootm 0x82000000
6. Once booted into OpenWrt, upload sysupgrade image to /tmp and flash:
     sysupgrade -n /tmp/openwrt-h3600-sysupgrade.bin

Reverting to Stock:

1. Boot into OpenWrt initramfs via TFTP as described above.
2. Write OEM kernel and rootfs partitions back to MTD partitions
   kernel_A and rootfs_A (or kernel_B and rootfs_B).
3. Reset bootloader boot_seq variable to 0.

MAC Address Layout:

LAN   : 34:E3:80:xx:xx:01 (mtd "tag", offset 0x1e)
WAN   : 34:E3:80:xx:xx:02 (mtd "tag", offset 0x1e + 1)
2.4GHz: 34:E3:80:xx:xx:03 (mtd "wifi", caldata file offset 0x4)
5GHz  : 34:E3:80:xx:xx:04 (mtd "wifi", caldata file offset 0x4 + 1)

Tested and Working:
- Sanechips ZX279128S target, SMP dual core, clocks, and timers
- All 5 GbE ports (4 LAN + 1 WAN) with line-rate flow offloading
- Optional hardware LAN switching via switch matrix bypass
- Dual-band 802.11ax Wi-Fi with PCIe L2C-310 cache synchronization
- SPI-NAND flash driver with JFFS2 cleanmarker OOB persistence
- Dual-partition sysupgrade matching vendor cspboot slot logic
- LEDs and physical push buttons

Signed-off-by: Navid Ghahremani <ghahramani.navid@gmail.com>
